+\nuseven{
+\vspace{1.5ex}
+Let $\InitialNSMValueBalance$ and $\NUSevenActivationHeight$ be as defined in \crossref{constants},
+and let $\NSMFeeContribution$ and $\AdditionalBlockSubsidy$ be as defined in \shortcrossref{subsidies}.
+
+\cite{ZIP-237} specifies a Network Sustainability Mechanism that tracks value removed from
+circulation and reissues it through the \blockSubsidy. The value removed from circulation in the
+\block at \blockHeight $\BlockHeight$ is $\NSMValueRemoved(\BlockHeight) := \NSMFeeContribution(\BlockHeight)$,
+the part of the \transactionFees specified by \cite{ZIP-235}, which is the only removal mechanism
+deployed in \NUSeven.
+
+The \defining{NSM Value Balance} of a \blockChain up to and including \blockHeight $\BlockHeight$
+is given by:
+
+\begin{formulae}
+  \item $\NSMValueBalance(\BlockHeight \typecolon \Nat) :=$
+        \vspace{-0.5ex}
+  \item \tab $\begin{cases}
+          0,&\caseif \BlockHeight < \NUSevenActivationHeight - 1 \\[0.6ex]
+          \InitialNSMValueBalance,&\caseif \BlockHeight = \NUSevenActivationHeight - 1 \\[0.6ex]
+          \NSMValueBalance(\BlockHeight - 1) - \AdditionalBlockSubsidy(\BlockHeight) \\[-0.4ex]
+          \hspace{1.5em} +\, \NSMValueRemoved(\BlockHeight),&\caseotherwise
+        \end{cases}$
+\end{formulae}
+
+\vspace{-2ex}
+\consensusrule{\nusevenonward{If $\NSMValueBalance(\BlockHeight)$ would become negative in the \blockChain
+created as a result of accepting a \block at \blockHeight $\BlockHeight$, then all nodes \MUST reject
+the block as invalid.}}
+
+\begin{pnotes}
+  \item The NSM Value Balance is tracked as consensus state alongside the \chainValuePools. It is
+        not a spendable \chainValuePool and is not included in $\IssuedSupply(\BlockHeight)$: it
+        counts \ZEC (or \TAZ) that is not in circulation. Reissuance moves value from the NSM Value
+        Balance into the \totalIssuedSupply through the \blockSubsidy.
+  \item As \cite{ZIP-2003} clarifies, the \SproutChainValuePool balance at \NUSeven activation
+        remains issued, and so is included in $\IssuedSupply(\BlockHeight)$ for the purposes of
+        \cite{ZIP-237}.
+\end{pnotes}
+} %nuseven
+
